    "result_text": "Done. The build passes green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe app now rejects a `POST /api/owners` whose supplied `registrationDate` is later than the server's current date, responding **400**, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection pattern:\n\n1. **`RequireRegistrationDateNotFuture`** (new function step) \u2014 reads the validated `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, and if `registrationDate` is present and `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`, throws a checked `FutureRegistrationDateException`. An absent date is accepted (it's optional and later defaults to today). The check uses the date exactly as supplied, before any business-day roll.\n\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML (`officefloor/escalation/\u2026FutureRegistrationDateException.yml`) \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing `InvalidPostcodeException` handler.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the new `registrationDate` step right after `require` (which publishes the DTO), before `postcode`, so an invalid future date is a 400 early in the pipeline.\n\nThe step runs before the transactional governance steps, so a rejected request never opens a write transaction.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsFutureDate` (posts `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"`, expects 400) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
